 16	/**
 17	 * The native raid estimator: samples the host's own battle engine as a read-only
 18	 * question.
 19	 *
 20	 * It is not a second battle implementation. Every run asks
 21	 * `simulateBattle($seed, true)` — the pure, seeded shape R1 added — on the engine
 22	 * the host itself fights with (`SettingsService::battleEngine()`), so the engine
 23	 * stays the authority on the rules and a "what if" never touches the world. Both
 24	 * engines are seeded: the Rust FFI carries the seed in its input and derives one
 25	 * stream per side per round, so a screen replays identically whichever engine the
 26	 * universe runs. Rust is roughly 7x faster per simulation, which is why the
 27	 * module no longer pins the PHP engine.
 28	 *
 29	 * The fleet is the account's own ships on the origin planet, and the defender is
 30	 * the host's stationary picture of the target planet, so no unit, price or
 31	 * defence figure is named here.
 32	 */
 33	class NativeRaidEstimator
 34	{
 35	    private const SCREEN_SAMPLES = 50;
 36	
 37	    private const CRYSTAL_WEIGHT = 1.5;
 38	
